# Site capabilities, not slug checks

New site behavior goes through [`src/lib/site-config.ts`](../../src/lib/site-config.ts). See [docs/site-architecture.md](../../docs/site-architecture.md).

```ts
// BAD
if (siteSlug === "side-sleeper") { ... }
if (siteSlug === "findworthnow") { ... }

// GOOD
if (siteHasFeature(site, "articles")) { ... }
if (getSiteTheme(site) === "paper") { ... }
if (getArticleConfig(site)?.route === "blog") { ... }
```

- `articles` is one content system. Public name/path come from `articleConfig` (`Reviews`/`/reviews` vs `Blog`/`/blog`), not from separate `blog`/`reviews` features.
- Catalog product reviews (`/{category}/{slug}`) are the `catalog` feature, not Articles.
- Themes (`default` | `paper` | `editorial-dark`) are presentation. Do not key CSS off slug.
- Templates/presets are start config only. Do not add `site.type === "findworthnow"`.
- The only slug→behavior table is `SITE_CAPABILITIES`. Do not scatter new slug checks.
